Z||000001||theogre||04-24-2000||10:48 PM||||I very strongly recomend you study copyright laws before you begin this project. If you pull information from the web to produce an even remotely comercial product without author permision you'll very likey end up in court. Some people don't care, others do. And like rock bands after Napster they likely won't diddle around with cease orders before filing. This includes information posted to this and other online forums. All rights to forum material are held either by the original author or the forum owner depending on the terms of service. I won't even get into the obvious things about pulling from other printed material.<P>Trademark law adds even more twists. If you use anything to do with Fiero trademarks in a comercial product without license from GM they can and likely will come after you. (There is a very long thread about one such GM action on the general forum I think.)<P>I've spent considerable time on the things I've written. I'm still studying how these laws effect my own work. My work is non comercial, but it's published thru this site wich can be considered comercial. Makes it even more interesting that this involves international law. I can't even begin to make sense of that. I can tell you for sure that if I found my stuff on another web site or in a comercial product without my permision the persons involved would not liket the results. I have hundreds of hours of time in just the things already posted here and in Tunnel #6. I have hundreds of hours more in the updates that are comming. Same goes for most of the rest of the better material on the web.<P>No, Cliff doesn't pay me to write here. He does give me a meg or 2 of space on a very popular server. That and the fact I can work with a guy I've never met on another continent are why my pages are here. Cliff and I respect each others copyrights and trademarks completely.<P>This isn't ment to sound stuffy or threatning. If you've never published anything then you need to be aware of all this. The U.S. "Digital Millenium Copyright" act has added even more confusion. ||||reg||1
